{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"winner\":\"A\",\"reason\":\"Deck A is stronger overall. A7 correctly places likelihood horizontally and impact vertically; B7 reverses the required axes, although its mitigation list preserves the values. A4 presents scenario paybacks and net savings in an easily compared table, while B4 uses repeated text and adds an unsupported claim that downside risk is bounded at $68k. A5 clearly distinguishes capacity-constrained sites from sites below the on-time gate; B5 preserves the required table and constrained-site names but communicates less of the operational implication. Both decks have readable charts, consistent formatting, complete financial figures on slides 1 and 8, and connected two-lane roadmaps on slide 6. A6's title accurately identifies validation and training as gate prerequisites, whereas B6's title says build and train despite its correct diagram. B's larger chart areas and clean white backgrounds are effective, but A generally offers more concise explanations and clearer hierarchy; B2's repeated data sentence crowds the footer, and B7's stacked vertical axis label is harder to read. These differences favor A beyond minor aesthetic preferences.\",\"dimensions\":{\"design\":\"tie\",\"legibility\":\"A\",\"visual_communication\":\"A\",\"coherence\":\"A\",\"requirements\":\"A\"}}"}}
